d{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A-I:$\n\n$$\n(A-I)v=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A-I:$\n\n$$\n(A-I)w=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A-I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A-I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A-I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $2$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $2$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =1$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070419/state.json" "file_sha256" "7675e59e53c101e2923daf8849f9d8b01deededeb97813dfa1e9905db5ff20d0"} {"question" "q-109525" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070419/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "a3f1d0e2bdbe34af20a523a05b939c7056afc42d4ad57f57464c26a385e82c3f"} {"question" "q-109525" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070419/state.json" "file_sha256" "7675e59e53c101e2923daf8849f9d8b01deededeb97813dfa1e9905db5ff20d0"} {"ques